From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luma: the Hotspot row uses the radio-tower glyph

Studio Desktop draws Hotspot with Lucide's radio-tower (its G() maps
hotspot to radio-tower). The system icon set provides it as
lumaui-radio-tower-symbolic; no set provides lumaui-hotspot-symbolic, so the
row had no glyph and the image's icon-reference check failed.

diff --git a/js/ui/quickSettings.js b/js/ui/quickSettings.js
index 109dc65..0a9a9d2 100644
--- a/js/ui/quickSettings.js
+++ b/js/ui/quickSettings.js
@@ -1509,7 +1509,7 @@ export const QuickSettingsMenu = class extends PopupMenu.PopupMenu {
             const hotspot = wifi._hotspot;
             if (hotspot) {
                 hotspot.get_parent()?.remove_child(hotspot);
-                const note = decorateStudioSwitchRow(hotspot, 'lumaui-hotspot-symbolic');
+                const note = decorateStudioSwitchRow(hotspot, 'lumaui-radio-tower-symbolic');
                 const syncHotspotCopy = () => {
                     note.text = hotspot.state ? _('Sharing this connection') : _('Share this connection');
                     note.visible = true;
